"ЦЮГРУНК\")\n50: \n51:         OcrTextCleaner.dictionaryCoverage(\"ЖЖУЗЛИК ЦЮГРУНК\") shouldBe 1f\n52:     }\n53: \n54:     @Test\n55:     fun `dictionaryCoverage drops to zero for invented words without user dict`() {\n56:         OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n57:         OcrTextCleaner.dictionaryCoverage(\"ЖЖУЗЛИК ЦЮГРУНК\") shouldBe 0f\n58:     }\n59: \n60:     @Test\n61:     fun `dictionaryCoverage stays zero for pure latin and sfx`() {\n62:         OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n63:         OcrTextCleaner.dictionaryCoverage(\"BAM!! 3D WI-FI\") shouldBe 0f\n64:     }\n65: \n66:     @Test\n67:     fun `user word hits are counted in stats for the scanner indicator`() {\n68:         OcrTextCleanerStats.reset()\n69:         OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n70:         OcrVocabulary.addWord(\"ЭРЗАЦ\")\n71: \n72:         OcrTextCleaner.knownWord(\"ЭРЗАЦ\") shouldBe true\n73:         OcrTextCleanerStats.wordDictHits shouldBe 0\n74:         OcrTextCleanerStats.userDictHits shouldBe 1\n75:     }\n76: \n77:     @Test\n78:     fun `knownWord returns true for user word even without builtin match`() {\n79:         OcrTextCleanerStats.reset()\n80:         OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n81: \n82:         OcrTextCleaner.knownWord(\"СЕГОДНЯ\") shouldBe true\n83:         OcrTextCleanerStats.userDictHits shouldBe 0\n84:     }\n85: }\n\n(End of file - total 85 lines)\n</content>", "metadata": {"preview": "package mihon.data.ocr\n\nimport io.kotest.matchers.floats.shouldBeLessThan\nimport io.kotest.matchers.shouldBe\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.AfterEach\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test\n\n/**\n * Пользовательский словарь в постобработке: разбиение слипшегося прогона и\n * покрытие для ранжирования кандидатов.\n *\n * Слова ЖЖУЗЛИК/ЦЮГРУНК выдуманы и отсутствуют во встроенном RuWordList\n * (подтверждено DP-проверкой: без пользовательского словаря прогон не\n * собирается в полное покрытие ни одним набором словарных сегментов).\n */\nclass OcrTextCleanerUserDictTest {\n\n    @AfterEach\n    fun tearDown() {\n        OcrVocabulary.configure(null)", "truncated": false, "loaded": [], "display": {"type": "file", "path": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code/data/src/test/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrTextCleanerUserDictTest.kt", "text": "package mihon.data.ocr\n\nimport io.kotest.matchers.floats.shouldBeLessThan\nimport io.kotest.matchers.shouldBe\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.AfterEach\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test\n\n/**\n * Пользовательский словарь в постобработке: разбиение слипшегося прогона и\n * покрытие для ранжирования кандидатов.\n *\n * Слова ЖЖУЗЛИК/ЦЮГРУНК выдуманы и отсутствуют во встроенном RuWordList\n * (подтверждено DP-проверкой: без пользовательского словаря прогон не\n * собирается в полное покрытие ни одним набором словарных сегментов).\n */\nclass OcrTextCleanerUserDictTest {\n\n    @AfterEach\n    fun tearDown() {\n        OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun `glued run splits using user dictionary words`() {\n        OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n        OcrVocabulary.addWord(\"ЖЖУЗЛИК\")\n        OcrVocabulary.addWord(\"ЦЮГРУНК\")\n\n        OcrTextCleaner.normalizeLocalCyrillicCaption(\"ЖЖУЗЛИКЦЮГРУНК\") shouldBe \"ЖЖУЗЛИК ЦЮГРУНК\"\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun `glued run stays intact without user words`() {\n        OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n        OcrTextCleaner.normalizeLocalCyrillicCaption(\"ЖЖУЗЛИКЦЮГРУНК\") shouldBe \"ЖЖУЗЛИКЦЮГРУНК\"\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun `user dictionary coverage does not include built-in words`() {\n        OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n\n        OcrTextCleaner.userDictionaryCoverage(\"Столичный город Арзия\") shouldBe 0f\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun `dictionaryCoverage counts user words as covered letters`() {\n        OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n        OcrVocabulary.addWord(\"ЖЖУЗЛИК\")\n        OcrVocabulary.addWord(\"ЦЮГРУНК\")\n\n        OcrTextCleaner.dictionaryCoverage(\"ЖЖУЗЛИК ЦЮГРУНК\") shouldBe 1f\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun `dictionaryCoverage drops to zero for invented words without user dict`() {\n        OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n        OcrTextCleaner.dictionaryCoverage(\"ЖЖУЗЛИК ЦЮГРУНК\") shouldBe 0f\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun `dictionaryCoverage stays zero for pure latin and sfx`() {\n        OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n        OcrTextCleaner.dictionaryCoverage(\"BAM!! 3D WI-FI\") shouldBe 0f\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun `user word hits are counted in stats for the scanner indicator`() {\n        OcrTextCleanerStats.reset()\n        OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n        OcrVocabulary.addWord(\"ЭРЗАЦ\")\n\n        OcrTextCleaner.knownWord(\"ЭРЗАЦ\") shouldBe true\n        OcrTextCleanerStats.wordDictHits shouldBe 0\n        OcrTextCleanerStats.userDictHits shouldBe 1\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun `knownWord returns true for user word even without builtin match`() {\n        OcrTextCleanerStats.reset()\n        OcrVocabulary.configure(null)\n\n        OcrTextCleaner.knownWord(\"СЕГОДНЯ\") shouldBe true\n        OcrTextCleanerStats.userDictHits shouldBe 0\n    }\n}", "lineStart": 1, "lineEnd": 85, "totalLines": 85, "truncated": false}}, "title": "data/src/test/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrTextCleanerUserDictTest.kt", "time": {"start": 1791916084868, "end": 1791916085329}}, "id": "prt_136858d92001r42g5GxW7awSPd", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136857d77001Dn9xDgYJ4J2CNi"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 26259, "input": 6493, "output": 259, "reasoning": 51, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 19456}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_1368592d60016KLoKUzehftjRN", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136857d77001Dn9xDgYJ4J2CNi"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136851e9f001vbQSM6Hp2bsA9j", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 32192, "input": 2949, "output": 475, "reasoning": 2912, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 25856}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791916088502, "completed": 1791916154956}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_136859cb60019wUfq5D8oncSxP", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13685abaa001XcpRHDr0u9Wf76", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136859cb60019wUfq5D8oncSxP"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Now let me implement. Plan:\n\n1. Generator: write hash-sharded asset files instead of one file. Let me decide the sharding scheme and the Java-compatible hash.\n\nBut wait — the generator can't run without the raw lexicon (OpenCorpora) which I likely don't have. So I can't regenerate `forms` from source. Instead, I should shard the **existing** `data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt`, which is already the final deduped/uppercased sorted list. I can write a small one-off sharding operation, and update `write_asset` in the generator to produce shards (so future regen works). But to shard now, I can just process the existing file.\n\nActually, does the generator's `build()` output match the existing asset exactly? It should, if run with the same lexicon. But I don't have the lexicon. So I'll shard the existing asset file directly (a one-off python), and also update the generator's `write_asset` → `write_shards` so it stays consistent for future runs.\n\nLet me design:\n- Shard dir: `data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words/`\n- Files: `%02x.txt` (00..ff), 256 shards.\n- Shard function: Java `String.hashCode()` low byte.\n\nJava hashCode:\n```python\ndef jhash(s):\n    h = 0\n    for ch in s:\n        h = (h * 31 + ord(ch)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    # interpret as signed 32-bit then take low byte; low byte same regardless\n    return h & 0xFF\n```\nLow byte = h & 0xFF. Good, no signedness issue.\n\n- Each shard file: uppercase wordforms, one per line, in any order (they'll be loaded into a HashSet). Keep sorted for reproducibility.\n- Runtime: `RuWordList.contains(word)`: shard = word.hashCode() and 0xFF; lazily load `ocr/ru_words/%02x.txt`.\n\nKotlin `word.hashCode()` = Java String hashCode. Low byte `(hashCode() and 0xFF)`. Matches.\n\nLet me now think about whether the runtime should uppercase the word. `justify`/callers already pass uppercase `up`. `knownWord` computes `up = word.uppercase()`. `OcrVocabulary.isKnownWord` computes `up`. So `contains` receives uppercase. Good. But to be safe, `contains` could uppercase internally? No — keep it requiring uppercase and document. Actually `knownWord` passes `up`; fine.\n\nNow, memory/caching: I'll cache loaded shards in a `HashMap<Int, Set<String>>` guarded by a lock. Each shard ~12k words. Over a session, if many shards load, memory grows, but no 3M spike. Good enough and matches \"chunks\".\n\nConcern: Loading a shard on first use within an OCR pass could cause a slight hiccup, but 12k inserts is ~1ms, negligible. And it's off the main thread (OCR runs in background).\n\nTest fallback: In JVM tests, no AssetManager. `configure` is called in App but not in tests. Tests call `OcrVocabulary.configure(null)` and rely on `RuWordList` falling back to file paths. So `RuWordList` needs a filesystem fallback reading from `data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words/%02x.txt` (cwd = data module dir). Keep `TEST_SOURCE_CANDIDATES` but for the dir. Let me implement `openShard(shard)`:\n- if opener != null: `context.assets.open(\"ocr/ru_words/%02x.txt\")`\n- else: for each candidate base dir (`src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words`, `data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words`), open file.\n\nI'll store the opener as a function of shard name.\n\nLet me write the new RuWordList.\n\n```kotlin\npackage mihon.data.ocr\n\nimport android.content.Context\nimport java.io.File\nimport java.io.InputStream\nimport logcat.LogPriority\nimport tachiyomi.core.common.util.system.logcat\n\nobject RuWordList {\n\n    private const val SHARD_DIR = \"ocr/ru_words\"\n    private const val SHARD_COUNT = 256\n\n    private val TEST_DIR_CANDIDATES = listOf(\n        \"src/main/assets/$SHARD_DIR\",\n        \"data/src/main/assets/$SHARD_DIR\",\n    )\n\n    @Volatile\n    private var opener: ((String) -> InputStream)? = null\n\n    private val lock = Any()\n    private val cache = HashMap<Int, Set<String>>()\n\n    fun configure(context: Context) {\n        opener = { name -> context.assets.open(\"$SHARD_DIR/$name\") }\n    }\n\n    /** Правда, если ПРОПИСНАЯ словоформа есть во встроенном словаре. */\n    fun contains(word: String): Boolean {\n        if (word.isEmpty()) return false\n        val shard = word.hashCode() and (SHARD_COUNT - 1)\n        return shardWords(shard).contains(word)\n    }\n\n    private fun shardWords(shard: Int): Set<String> {\n        synchronized(lock) { cache[shard]?.let { return it } }\n        val name = \"%02x.txt\".format(shard)\n        val words = loadShard(name)\n        synchronized(lock) {\n            cache[shard]?.let { return it }\n            cache[shard] = words\n            return words\n        }\n    }\n\n    private fun loadShard(name: String): Set<String> {\n        val stream = openShard(name)\n        if (stream == null) {\n            logcat(LogPriority.WARN) {\n                \"RuWordList: чанк $SHARD_DIR/$name не найден — разбиение капса деградирует\"\n            }\n            return emptySet()\n        }\n        val set = HashSet<String>()\n        stream.bufferedReader(Charsets.UTF_8).use { reader ->\n            while (true) {\n                val line = reader.readLine() ?: break\n                if (line.isNotEmpty()) set.add(line)\n            }\n        }\n        return set\n    }\n\n    private fun openShard(name: String): InputStream? {\n        opener?.let { return it(name) }\n        for (dir in TEST_DIR_CANDIDATES) {\n            val file = File(dir, name)\n            if (file.isFile) return file.inputStream()\n        }\n        return null\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWait: `\"%02x.txt\".format(shard)` — Kotlin `String.format` uses `String.format(this, args)`. Fine. But Locale? Hex has no locale issue.\n\nNow I'm caching emptySet for missing shard → returns emptySet → contains false. Fine, and avoids repeated open attempts.\n\nBut caching emptySet when asset genuinely missing means OCR degrades but doesn't repeatedly warn. Good.\n\nNow update call sites:\n- `OcrTextCleaner.kt:468`: `return RuWordList.contains(up)`.\n- `OcrVocabulary.kt:137`: `if (RuWordList.contains(up)) return true`.\n\nNow generator: change `write_asset` to `write_shards` writing 256 files, and delete the single file. Also `main()` message.\n\nLet me implement the generator sharding with Java-compatible hash.\n\n```python\nSHARD_DIR_REL = \"data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words\"\nSHARD_COUNT = 256\n\ndef _jhash(word):\n    h = 0\n    for ch in word:\n        h = (h * 31 + ord(ch)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    return h & (SHARD_COUNT - 1)\n\ndef write_shards(repo, forms):\n    out_dir = os.path.join(repo, SHARD_DIR_REL)\n    os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    shards = {}\n    for word in forms:\n        up = word.upper()\n        shards.setdefault(_jhash(up), []).append(up)\n    # clean old shard files\n    for fname in os.listdir(out_dir):\n        if fname.endswith(\".txt\"):\n            os.remove(os.path.join(out_dir, fname))\n    for shard, words in shards.items():\n        words.sort()\n        with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f\"{shard:02x}.txt\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\\n\") as handle:\n            for w in words:\n                handle.write(w + \"\\n\")\n```\n\nWait: shard based on uppercase word — runtime computes hashCode of the uppercase word it receives. Good, must shard on uppercased form. Yes, I use `up = word.upper()` then hash `up`. But the earlier asset wrote `word.upper()` where `word` was lowercased forms. `forms` from `build()` is lowercased (with е). `.upper()` maps е→Е, ё already replaced. Note: Python `str.upper()` on \"е\" → \"Е\", and there's no ё. Fine, same as before.\n\nHmm wait, subtle: runtime receives `up = word.uppercase()` (Kotlin). For a word containing \"ё\", Kotlin uppercase → \"Ё\". But the asset was built from forms where ё was replaced by е (`build()` does `f.replace(\"ё\",\"е\")`), then `.upper()` → \"Е\". And `with_yo_variants` added ё variants during build, but then line 110 replaces ё→е for all forms. So no \"Ё\" in the dictionary at all. Runtime `word.uppercase()` of a caption token like \"намёка\" → \"НАМЁКА\" (Ё). That would NOT match \"НАМЕКА\". Hmm, but this behavior is pre-existing (the asset is all-Е). Let me check OcrTextCleaner: does it normalize ё→е before lookup? `knownWord` does `word.uppercase()` without ё normalization. So \"НАМЁКА\" wouldn't match. But the asset also contains... only Е forms. So match would fail for ё words. This is pre-existing behavior, not something I'm changing. The docstring claimed ё/е variants are included, but line 110 collapses them. Not my concern now; don't change semantics.\n\nActually wait, this matters for sharding correctness only in that runtime hash and generation hash must agree. Runtime hashes the uppercased token as-is (possibly with Ё). Generation hashes the uppercased form (with Е). If runtime token has Ё, its hash maps to a different shard than Е; but Е and Ё are different code points → different hash anyway → different shard. But since the dictionary contains no Ё words, even if it landed in a shard we'd look in the Ё-shard and not find Е-words there → correctly not found (consistent with no match). Actually if we look up \"НАМЁКА\", its hash → some shard; we load that shard (which may contain unrelated words); \"НАМЁКА\" not present → false. Correct (no false positive). Good, no correctness issue introduced.\n\nNow the concern: does sharding change any existing test expectation? Tests rely on dictionary lookups. The hash must match between Python and Kotlin. Let me verify with a quick check after generating: pick a few words, compute Python shard and Kotlin shard. I'll compile a tiny test? Easier: I'll write a quick JVM check via a unit test? Or reason: Java hashCode formula implemented identically. I'm fairly confident.\n\nBut to be safe, I can verify by having Python emit a small expected file and a Kotlin test? Overkill. Instead, I can trust the standard algorithm and then run the existing OCR tests (OcrTextCleanerTest 37, etc.) which heavily exercise the dictionary. If hashing mismatched, tests would fail (dictionary effectively empty → splits fail). So the test suite is the verification. \n\nNow, there's another concern: the existing `ru_wordlist.txt` single asset — should I keep it or remove it? If I keep it, it bloats APK ~11MB (unused). Remove it. But other code/tests reference it? Grep showed only RuWordList.kt references ASSET_PATH. Tests use RuWordList via fallback. So remove the file.\n\nAlso update the KDoc in RuWordList and generator.\n\nAlso `App.kt` configure call remains valid (configure signature unchanged: Context).\n\nNow, the test fallback path: cwd for `:data` tests is the `data` module dir, so `src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words/` works. Good.\n\nLet me now also double check: `word.hashCode()` in Kotlin returns Int; `and 0xFF` gives 0..255. `SHARD_COUNT - 1 = 255`. Good.\n\nLet me implement.\n\nSteps:\n1. Write sharding of existing asset into 256 files, remove single file.\n2. Rewrite RuWordList.kt.\n3. Update generator.\n4. Update 2 call sites.\n5. Compile + test.\n\nLet me do step 1 with python, and also verify shard sizes.\n\nActually, I'll write the sharding script inline, but also the generator must produce the same. Let me just do the one-off python now, and separately update the generator file.\n\nLet me run the sharding.", "time": {"start": 1791916092436, "end": 1791916110478}, "id": "prt_13685ac14001VwQVB0MkqCLQ8t", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136859cb60019wUfq5D8oncSxP"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Реализую. Режу существующий ассет на 256 шардов по Java-`hashCode()`, чтобы рантайм лениво грузил только нужные чанки.", "time": {"start": 1791916110499, "end": 1791916112501}, "id": "prt_13685f2a3001vZBX7TsHUxmAM0", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136859cb60019wUfq5D8oncSxP"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_du980q26plycai38tjxxhct5", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport os, shutil\nSRC = 'data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt'\nOUT = 'data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words'\nN = 256\ndef jhash(word):\n    h = 0\n    for ch in word:\n        h = (h * 31 + ord(ch)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    return h & (N - 1)\nshards = {}\ntotal = 0\nwith open(SRC, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for line in f:\n        w = line.rstrip('\\n')\n        if not w:\n            continue\n        shards.setdefault(jhash(w), []).append(w)\n        total += 1\nos.makedirs(OUT, exist_ok=True)\nfor fn in os.listdir(OUT):\n    if fn.endswith('.txt'):\n        os.remove(os.path.join(OUT, fn))\nsizes = []\nfor shard, words in shards.items():\n    words.sort()\n    sizes.append(len(words))\n    with open(os.path.join(OUT, f'{shard:02x}.txt'), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='\\n') as h:\n        h.write('\\n'.join(words) + '\\n')\nprint('total', total, 'shards', len(shards), 'min', min(sizes), 'max', max(sizes), 'avg', round(total/len(shards),1))\n# sanity: a few words\nfor w in ['НАМЕКА','СЕГОДНЯ','ГОДЫ','А','Я']:\n    print(w, f'{jhash(w):02x}')\nprint('files:', len([f for f in os.listdir(OUT) if f.endswith('.txt')]))\nEOF"}, "output": "total 3014492 shards 256 min 11430 max 12095 avg 11775.4\nНАМЕКА 82\nСЕГОДНЯ e7\nГОДЫ 42\nА 10\nЯ 2f\nfiles: 256\n", "metadata": {"output": "total 3014492 shards 256 min 11430 max 12095 avg 11775.4\nНАМЕКА 82\nСЕГОДНЯ e7\nГОДЫ 42\nА 10\nЯ 2f\nfiles: 256\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport os, shutil\nSRC = 'data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt'\nOUT = 'data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words'\nN = 256\ndef jhash(word):\n    h = 0\n    for ch in word:\n        h = (h * 31 + ord(ch)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    return h & (N - 1)\nshards = {}\ntotal = 0\nwith open(SRC, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for line in f:\n        w = line.rstrip('\\n')\n        if not w:\n            continue\n        shards.setdefault(jhash(w), []).append(w)\n        total += 1\nos.makedirs(OUT, exist_ok=True)\nfor fn in os.listdir(OUT):\n    if fn.endswith('.txt'):\n        os.remove(os.path.join(OUT, fn))\nsizes = []\nfor shard, words in shards.items():\n    words.sort()\n    sizes.append(len(words))\n    with open(os.path.join(OUT, f'{shard:02x}.txt'), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='\\n') as h:\n        h.write('\\n'.join(words) + '\\n')\nprint('total', total, 'shards', len(shards), 'min', min(sizes), 'max', max(sizes), 'avg', round(total/len(shards),1))\n# sanity: a few words\nfor w in ['НАМЕКА','СЕГОДНЯ','ГОДЫ','А','Я']:\n    print(w, f'{jhash(w):02x}')\nprint('files:', len([f for f in os.listdir(OUT) if f.endswith('.txt')]))\nEOF", "time": {"start": 1791916112458, "end": 1791916148748}}, "id": "prt_13685f3a7001FQmaBHg2nmnEEw", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136859cb60019wUfq5D8oncSxP"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "7c5c3cbb3e9272da652cf249e371e302a4b5b0de", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 32192, "input": 2949, "output": 475, "reasoning": 2912, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 25856}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_136869f24001CbGdQQYab9ZF63", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136859cb60019wUfq5D8oncSxP"}, {"type": "patch", "hash": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "files": ["/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code/data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words/00.txt", "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code/data/src/main/ass