"cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 57595, "input": 457, "output": 234, "reasoning": 712, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 56192}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791917344591, "completed": 1791917373455}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_13698c74f001ov379ivbFohso1", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "987f5222a8cb9fb60ba776cc5d813ddbf036b865", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13698d948001Zfqa08y4NQXCbK", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13698c74f001ov379ivbFohso1"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Interesting! The compressed total for ru_words is only 507,136 bytes (495 KB)?! And uncompressed 71,110,950. That's a compression ratio of ~140x. Wait — that means each shard (280,659 bytes) compressed to ~1,981 bytes?? That seems too good. Oh! Because each shard is sorted, and the words are similar... no, 140x is suspicious. Wait, maybe unzip -l columns: first column is uncompressed length, second is... actually `unzip -l` output columns are: Length (uncompressed), Date, Time, Name. There's no compressed column in `unzip -l`! The second number I treated as compressed is actually the date (1981-01-01). Let me re-read.\n\n`unzip -l` format:\n```\n  Length      Date    Time    Name\n---------  ---------- -----   ----\n   280659  1981-01-01 01:01   assets/ocr/ru_words/00.txt\n```\nSo `$1`=Length (uncompressed), `$2`=Date, `$3`=Time. My awk summed date as compressed → 507136 is sum of dates nonsense. So actual compressed size unknown from this. Need `unzip -v` which shows both Length and Compressed? Actually `unzip -v` columns: Length, Method, Size, Cmpr, Date, Time, CRC-32, Name. Let me use `unzip -v`.\n\nAlso debug APK size dropped from 107,767,032 to 118,702,809? Wait, it INCREASED? Earlier single-asset debug was 107,767,032. Now 118,702,809 — larger by ~11MB! That suggests the single asset (compressed ~11.3MB) was removed but now 256 shards compressed to... something larger? Or the earlier measurement was different.\n\nWait, earlier I recorded \"app-arm64-v8a-debug.apk = 107,767,032 bytes (103MB). Asset inside APK: assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt 71,110,950 stored → Defl:N 11,340,327\". Hmm, that earlier debug included the single asset (11.3MB compressed). Now debug is 118.7MB. So removing the single 11.3MB asset but adding 256 shards totaling ~? If total shards compressed < 11.3MB, size should drop. It grew by 11MB, meaning shards compressed to ~22MB? That doesn't make sense either.\n\nHold on — maybe the earlier debug build didn't have the OCR models/assets but this build does, or there's variance. Or maybe the two builds differ because `assembleDebug` now packaged more (e.g., native libs). Actually, maybe the earlier 107MB figure was from a build before I added RuWordList.configure or before something. Hard to say.\n\nLet me get accurate compressed sizes with `unzip -v`.\n\nActually wait — there's another possibility: debug APK 118.7MB vs release 87MB. The release shrinks with R8. Debug doesn't. The comparison that matters is release. But I need the compressed size of shards.\n\nLet me run `unzip -v` and sum Size (compressed).", "time": {"start": 1791917349330, "end": 1791917354966}, "id": "prt_13698d9d2001BD78e7Yx2qimPb", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13698c74f001ov379ivbFohso1"}, {"type": "text", "text": "`unzip -l` не показывает сжатый размер — беру `unzip -v`:", "time": {"start": 1791917354969, "end": 1791917355284}, "id": "prt_13698efd9001Zfi6dm59rHdKQd", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13698c74f001ov379ivbFohso1"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_dkohhcgu18q63vbc5liro1mq", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && APK=app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-arm64-v8a-debug.apk && unzip -v \"$APK\" | grep \"assets/ocr/ru_words/\" | awk '{c+=$3; u+=$1} END {print \"shards:\", NR, \"uncompressed=\"u,