0768 89203 classes3.dex\n119668 30839 classes33.dex\n64612 28723 classes34.dex\n25047232 8578647 classes35.dex\n11050684 4616078 classes36.dex\n10628832 4114438 classes37.dex\n14330360 5449399 classes38.dex\n6597312 2774773 classes39.dex\n555444 229121 classes4.dex\n42924 17106 classes5.dex\n214860 93172 classes6.dex\n95776 38078 classes7.dex\n105808 42572 classes9.dex\n1597520 632252 classes12.dex\n867316 321691 classes18.dex\n1482372 529486 classes19.dex\n1182812 503567 classes20.dex\n678348 267125 classes21.dex\n739748 281998 classes22.dex\n1746548 669447 classes23.dex\n491508 192928 classes24.dex\n1501096 569910 classes25.dex\n2005460 748718 classes26.dex\n1844036 768801 classes27.dex\n1692428 627666 classes28.dex\n1371260 520305 classes29.dex\n1106916 408561 classes30.dex\n1436924 544050 classes31.dex\n1427084 541877 classes32.dex\n254528 102931 classes8.dex\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && APK=app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-arm64-v8a-debug.apk && unzip -v \"$APK\" | grep \"assets/ocr/ru_words/\" | awk '{c+=$3; u+=$1} END {print \"shards:\", NR, \"uncompressed=\"u, \"compressed=\"c, \"ratio=\"u/c}' && echo \"--- any leftover single asset? ---\" && unzip -l \"$APK\" | grep \"ocr/ru_wordlist\" || echo \"none (good)\" && echo \"--- dex/classes sizes ---\" && unzip -v \"$APK\" | grep -E \"classes[0-9]*\\.dex\" | awk '{print $1, $3, $8}'", "time": {"start": 1791917355249, "end": 1791917355486}}, "id": "prt_13698efe5001bMNs3h96QLSsIB", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13698c74f001ov379ivbFohso1"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "987f5222a8cb9fb60ba776cc5d813ddbf036b865", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 57595, "input": 457, "output": 234, "reasoning": 712, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 56192}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_136993735001xDT5TGiZMt64lD", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13698c74f001ov379ivbFohso1"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136851e9f001vbQSM6Hp2bsA9j", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 60269, "input": 1487, "output": 548, "reasoning": 1658, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 56576}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791917375634, "completed": 1791917436775}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_136994092001h8jBpjRqdnG5oT", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "987f5222a8cb9fb60ba776cc5d813ddbf036b865", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13699575d0016uz2QmwFMOhVdE", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136994092001h8jBpjRqdnG5oT"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Now the shards compressed total = 22,004,815 bytes (~22 MB), whereas the single sorted file compressed to 11,340,327 (~11.3 MB). So sharding by hash DESTROYED cross-file compression! Because each shard has random words (by hash), within-file redundancy is low, and more importantly the whole-file compression benefited from shared substrings/delta across alphabetically-sorted neighbors. Splitting into 256 hash shards lost ~10.6MB. That's bad — it eats half the savings.\n\nWait, why? A single sorted file of 3M similar words compresses extremely well (long common prefixes between adjacent words → deflate finds repeated substrings). Hash shards scramble adjacency → each word is isolated → much worse compression. Each shard ~278KB uncompressed → ~86KB compressed = 3.2x. The single sorted file 71MB → 11.3MB = 6.3x. So yes, sorting matters for compression.\n\nSo the goal (chunked lazy load) conflicts with compression (needs locality). To get both: shard by **sorted ranges** (contiguous chunks of the sorted list), not by hash. Then adjacency is preserved within each chunk, compression stays good, and chunks are even in size (fixed count of words each). Runtime lookup then needs to find WHICH chunk a word belongs to, which requires an index of chunk boundaries.\n\nDesign: split sorted list into N contiguous chunks of ~equal word count. To look up a word, need to know its chunk. Since chunks are ordered by the same lexicographic order as the words, we can binary-search the chunk boundaries: the index file stores the first word of each chunk (N entries). To find the chunk for `word`, find the largest boundary <= word. Then load that chunk and HashSet-contains.\n\nThat's clean:\n- Generator writes `ru_words/00.txt`..`NN.txt` as contiguous sorted ranges + `ru_words/index.txt` with one boundary word per chunk (first word of each chunk), in order.\n- Runtime loads index (small, N entries), binary-searches it to pick the chunk, lazily loads the chunk HashSet, then contains.\n\nCompression: each chunk sorted → good compression (~similar to whole file). Total should be ~11-13MB. Slight per-file overhead but minimal.\n\nIndex file: N lines, each the first word of chunk i. For N=256, that's tiny (~3KB). Runtime parses into an Array<String>.\n\nLookup:\n```\nfun contains(word):\n  idx = upperBound(boundaries, word) - 1   // boundaries[i] <= word\n  if idx < 0 -> false\n  load chunk idx -> HashSet.contains(word)\n```\nboundaries sorted ascending (since chunks are ordered and first words increase). Binary search fine.\n\nActually need care: the index word equals the first word of chunk; `boundaries[i] <= word`. Use binary search for rightmost boundary <= word.\n\nChunk size: with N=256, ~11,775 words/chunk. Chunk compressed ~ 71MB/256=278KB uncompressed → sorted chunk compresses ~ maybe 45KB each? Let me just regenerate contiguous chunks and measure.\n\nWait, but for compression, is it better to have FEWER, LARGER chunks? Larger = better compression ratio (more context). But lazy loading wants small chunks. Trade-off. 256 contiguous chunks of 11.7k sorted words each: within-chunk adjacency preserved, so ratio close to whole-file. Let me test.\n\nActually the whole file ratio 6.3x. A 278KB sorted slice should compress similarly (~6x) → ~46KB each × 256 = 11.8MB. Good, close to 11.3MB. Slight overhead. Acceptable.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: deflate window is 32KB. Long-range matches beyond 32KB aren't captured anyway, so the whole-file 6.3x comes from local (within-32KB) redundancy — which is preserved in contiguous chunks. So contiguous chunking should keep essentially the full ratio. \n\nLet me redo: generate contiguous chunks + index. Update RuWordList to load index + binary search. Update generator.\n\nLet me implement.\n\nGenerator:\n```python\ndef write_shards(repo, forms):\n    out_dir = ...\n    clear *.txt\n    CHUNK = (len(forms) + SHARD_COUNT - 1) // SHARD_COUNT\n    boundaries = []\n    for i in range(SHARD_COUNT):\n        chunk = forms[i*CHUNK:(i+1)*CHUNK]\n        if not chunk: break\n        boundaries.append(chunk[0].upper())\n        write f\"{i:02x}.txt\" lines chunk uppercased\n    write index.txt = boundaries joined by \\n\n```\nWait, forms are lowercased. Upper for writing and boundary. Since uppercase is monotonic with lowercase for Cyrillic (А..Я order preserved), boundaries remain sorted. Good.\n\nRuntime RuWordList:\n```kotlin\nprivate const val INDEX_NAME = \"index.txt\"\n@Volatile private var boundaries: Array<String>? = null  // lazy\nprivate val chunkCache = HashMap<Int, Set<String>>()\n\nfun contains(word):\n  if empty false\n  val b = boundaries()\n  if (b.isEmpty()) return false\n  val idx = floorIndex(b, word)\n  if (idx < 0) return false\n  return chunkWords(idx).contains(word)\n\nprivate fun floorIndex(b, word): Int {\n  var lo=0; hi=b.size-1; var ans=-1\n  while(lo<=hi){ mid; if (b[mid] <= word) {ans=mid; lo=mid+1} else hi=mid-1 }\n  return ans\n}\n```\nString comparison `b[mid] <= word` uses Kotlin natural String compareTo = UTF-16 code unit order. Python sorted uses code point order. For BMP (all our chars), UTF-16 code unit order == code point order. Cyrillic and '-' are BMP. Equal. Good.\n\nNow the index also needs to be loaded lazily and thread-safe. Let me load boundaries lazily with synchronized.\n\nAlso the test fallback dir must contain index.txt.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nLet me also double-check: the previous hash shards must be replaced. I'll regenerate.\n\nLet me implement generator first, run it against the existing... but wait, the single `ru_wordlist.txt` was deleted. I need `forms` (lowercased) to regenerate. I can reconstruct by reading the current 256 hash-shard files (uppercase) and lowercasing. Or better: do the contiguous split directly from the current shards' combined content. Since hash shards together = the full set; I can read all, lowercase, sort, then contiguous-chunk. That reproduces forms. Let me do a one-off python to generate contiguous chunks + index from the union of current shards, and also update generator for future.\n\nActually cleaner: I still have the union in the 256 hash files. Let me just read them all, build sorted list, and write contiguous chunks. Let me do that now, then update the generator to match.\n\nLet me write the one-off.\n\nThen test compression via assembleDebug again (expensive ~5min). Hmm. I could estimate by zipping the files. Let me create a test zip to measure, or use python zlib to sum compressed sizes. Python zlib with level 9 approximates deflate. But Android's APK uses deflate; let me just trust and verify via assembleDebug at the end.\n\nActually, I can measure with `zip`/python quickly: compress each chunk with zlib level 9 and sum. Let me do that as a quick estimate.\n\nLet me implement.", "time": {"start": 1791917381536, "end": 1791917394173}, "id": "prt_1369957a0001FgdWkoIQbt2iLs", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136994092001h8jBpjRqdnG5oT"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Проблема: хеш-шарды ломают сжатие — суммарно 22 МБ вместо 11.3 МБ, потому что рядом оказываются несвязанные слова. Перехожу на **непрерывные отсортированные чанки + индекс границ**: O(1)-поиск сохраняется (бинарный поиск по 256 границам), а локальность для deflate не теряется.", "time": {"start": 1791917394181, "end": 1791917396650}, "id": "prt_136998905001lAeb2BTfvzhx20", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136994092001h8jBpjRqdnG5oT"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_ltuosj9qrnj8eghpkw01gyu3", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport os, zlib\nSRC = 'data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words'\nN = 256\nwords = []\nfor fn in sorted(os.listdir(SRC)):\n    if fn.endswith('.txt'):\n        with open(os.path.join(SRC, fn), encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            words.extend(w for w in (l.rstrip('\\n') for l in f) if w)\nwords = sorted(set(words))\nprint(\"total words:\", len(words))\nchunk = (len(words) + N - 1) // N\n# clear dir\nfor fn in os.listdir(SRC):\n    if fn.endswith('.txt'):\n        os.remove(os.path.join(SRC, fn))\nboundaries = []\ncomp = 0\nfor i in range(N):\n    part = words[i*chunk:(i+1)*chunk]\n    if not part:\n        break\n    boundaries.append(part[0])\n    data = ('\\n'.join(part) + '\\n').encode('utf-8')\n    comp += len(zlib.compress(data, 9))\n    with open(os.path.join(SRC, f'{i:02x}.txt'), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='\\n') as h:\n        h.write('\\n'.join(part) + '\\n')\nwith open(os.path.join(SRC, 'index.txt'), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='\\n') as h:\n    h.write('\\n'.join(boundaries) + '\\n')\nprint(\"chunks:\", len(boundaries), \"chunk size:\", chunk)\nprint(\"zlib9 compressed sum (estimate):\", comp, \"bytes =\", round(comp/1024/1024,2), \"MB\")\nprint(\"first boundaries:\", boundaries[:3], \"...\", boundaries[-2:])\nEOF"}, "output": "total words: 3014492\nchunks: 256 chunk size: 11776\nzlib9 compressed sum (estimate): 8761916 bytes = 8.36 MB\nfirst boundaries: ['А', 'АБЛАКУЛ', 'АВТОГАЗОВ'] ... ['ЭНДОКРИНОЛОГА', 'ЮЖНОСАХАЛИНКЕ']\n", "metadata": {"output": "total words: 3014492\nchunks: 256 chunk size: 11776\nzlib9 compressed sum (estimate): 8761916 bytes = 8.36 MB\nfirst boundaries: ['А', 'АБЛАКУЛ', 'АВТОГАЗОВ'] ... ['ЭНДОКРИНОЛОГА', 'ЮЖНОСАХАЛИНКЕ']\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport os, zlib\nSRC = 'data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_words'\nN = 256\nwords = []\nfor fn in sorted(os.listdir(SRC)):\n    if fn.endswith('.txt'):\n        with open(os.path.join(SRC, fn), encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            words.extend(w for w in (l.rstrip('\\n') for l in f) if w)\nwords = sorted(set(words))\nprint(\"total words:\", len(words))\nchunk = (len(words) + N - 1) // N\n# clear dir\nfor fn in os.listdir(SRC):\n    if fn.endswith('.txt'):\n        os.remove(os.path.join(SRC, fn))\nboundaries = []\ncomp = 0\nfor i in range(N):\n    part = words[i*chunk:(i+1)*chunk]\n    if not part:\n        break\n    boundaries.append(part[0])\n    data = ('\\n'.join(part) + '\\n').encode('utf-8')\n    comp += len(zlib.compress(data, 9))\n    with open(os.path.join(SRC, f'{i:02x}.txt'), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='\\n') as h:\n        h.write('\\n'.join(part) + '\\n')\nwith open(os.path.join(SRC, 'index.txt'), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='\\n') as h:\n    h.write('\\n'.join(boundaries) + '\\n')\nprint(\"chunks:\", len(boundaries), \"chunk size:\", chunk)\nprint(\"zlib9 compressed sum (estimate):\", comp, \"bytes =\", round(comp/1024/1024,2), \"MB\")\nprint(\"first boundaries:\", boundaries[:3], \"...\", boundaries[-2:])\nEOF", "time": {"start": 1791917396632, "end": 1791917433994}}, "id": "prt_136998915001ufUMtkqj4bdTep", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136994092001h8jBpjRqdnG5oT"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "98430fbf31cd74f188ff9b9a9af47095c8b1417a", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 60269, "input": 1487, "output": 548, "reasoning": 1658, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 56576}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_1369a2ea1001jrtW8FuGyW9RAq", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465ff